From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winmm: MCI_OPEN with element name and element id

Opening with both MCI_OPEN_ELEMENT and MCI_OPEN_ELEMENT_ID returns
MCIERR_FLAGS_NOT_COMPATIBLE (the mcicda conformance test) instead of logging a
FIXME and MCIERR_UNRECOGNIZED_KEYWORD.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winmm/mci.c b/dlls/winmm/mci.c
index 46c21f8..ec7df90 100644
--- a/dlls/winmm/mci.c
+++ b/dlls/winmm/mci.c
@@ -1876,8 +1876,12 @@ static	DWORD MCI_Open(DWORD dwParam, LPMCI_OPEN_PARMSW lpParms)
 	TRACE("lpstrElementName=%s\n", debugstr_w(lpParms->lpstrElementName));
 
 	if (dwParam & MCI_OPEN_ELEMENT_ID) {
-	    FIXME("Unsupported yet flag MCI_OPEN_ELEMENT_ID\n");
+	    /* an element name and an element id exclude each other */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_MCI_ELEMENT_ID
 	    dwRet = MCIERR_UNRECOGNIZED_KEYWORD;
+#else
+	    dwRet = MCIERR_FLAGS_NOT_COMPATIBLE;
+#endif
 	    goto errCleanUp;
 	}
 
